### ============================================
### REDIS CACHE TESTING - Showtimes & Seat Availability
### ============================================
### Test all cached endpoints and verify cache behavior
### Note: First request = DB hit (slower), Second request = Cache hit (faster)

### ============================================
### 1. SHOWTIME ENDPOINTS - Cache Testing
### ============================================

### GET /showtimes - All showtimes (TTL: 60s)
### Run this TWICE: First = DB, Second = Cache
GET {{apiUrl}}/showtimes

### GET /showtimes - Second request (should be cached, faster)
GET {{apiUrl}}/showtimes

### GET /showtimes/movie/:movieId - Showtimes by movie (TTL: 60s)
### Run this TWICE: First = DB, Second = Cache
GET {{apiUrl}}/showtimes/movie/{{movie_id}}

### GET /showtimes/movie/:movieId - Second request (should be cached)
GET {{apiUrl}}/showtimes/movie/{{movie_id}}

### GET /showtimes/theater/:theaterId - Showtimes by theater (TTL: 60s)
### Note: Fill @theater_id from a showtime response first
### Run this TWICE: First = DB, Second = Cache
GET {{apiUrl}}/showtimes/theater/{{theater_id}}

### GET /showtimes/theater/:theaterId - Second request (should be cached)
GET {{apiUrl}}/showtimes/theater/{{theater_id}}

### GET /showtimes/:id - Single showtime (TTL: 5min)
### Run this TWICE: First = DB, Second = Cache
GET {{apiUrl}}/showtimes/{{showtime_id}}

### GET /showtimes/:id - Second request (should be cached)
GET {{apiUrl}}/showtimes/{{showtime_id}}

### GET /showtimes/:id/seats - Seat availability (TTL: 15s) - MOST CRITICAL
### Run this TWICE: First = DB, Second = Cache (should be MUCH faster)
GET {{apiUrl}}/showtimes/{{showtime_id}}/seats

### GET /showtimes/:id/seats - Second request (should be cached, very fast)
GET {{apiUrl}}/showtimes/{{showtime_id}}/seats

### ============================================
### 2. MOVIE SHOWTIMES ENDPOINT - Cache Testing
### ============================================

### GET /movies/:id/showtimes - Movie showtimes (TTL: 60s)
### Run this TWICE: First = DB, Second = Cache
GET {{apiUrl}}/movies/{{movie_id}}/showtimes

### GET /movies/:id/showtimes - Second request (should be cached)
GET {{apiUrl}}/movies/{{movie_id}}/showtimes

### GET /movies/:id/showtimes - With date filter
GET {{apiUrl}}/movies/{{movie_id}}/showtimes?date=2024-12-20

### GET /movies/:id/showtimes - With theater filter
GET {{apiUrl}}/movies/{{movie_id}}/showtimes?theater_id={{theater_id}}

### ============================================
### 3. CACHE INVALIDATION TESTING
### ============================================
### These operations should invalidate related caches

### Step 1: Get seat availability (cache it)
GET {{apiUrl}}/showtimes/{{showtime_id}}/seats

### Step 2: Create a booking (should invalidate seat availability cache)
POST {{apiUrl}}/bookings
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "user_id": "{{user_id}}",
  "showtime_id": "{{showtime_id}}",
  "seat_ids": ["{{seat_id1}}"]
}

### Step 3: Get seat availability again (should hit DB, not cache, because cache was invalidated)
### The available seats count should be reduced by 1
GET {{apiUrl}}/showtimes/{{showtime_id}}/seats

### Step 4: Reserve seats (should invalidate seat availability cache)
POST {{apiUrl}}/bookings/reserve
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "user_id": "{{user_id}}",
  "showtime_id": "{{showtime_id}}",
  "seat_ids": ["{{seat_id2}}"]
}

### Step 5: Get seat availability again (should hit DB, cache invalidated)
GET {{apiUrl}}/showtimes/{{showtime_id}}/seats

### Step 6: Cancel booking (should invalidate seat availability cache)
### Note: Make sure @booking_id is set from a previous booking
PUT {{apiUrl}}/bookings/{{booking_id}}/cancel
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "reason": "Testing cache invalidation"
}

### Step 7: Get seat availability again (should hit DB, seats released)
GET {{apiUrl}}/showtimes/{{showtime_id}}/seats

